# deploy-excludes.txt is read by `rsync --exclude-from` on an ubuntu-latest
# runner. rsync does not strip a trailing CR, so a CRLF checkout turns every
# pattern into "assets/dump\r", which matches nothing -- the deploy would then
# silently ship all the source material again while reporting success. Pin LF.
#
# Deliberately scoped to this one file. The workflows and shell scripts here
# already run fine as they are; renormalising them is a separate change with a
# much larger diff, and this file is the one where the failure is silent.
deploy-excludes.txt text eol=lf
